[patterns/application/extensions/PTN-APP-EXT-008-compatibility-testing-pattern.md#pattern-description]

### Pattern Description

This pattern establishes automated compatibility testing at multiple levels:

**Level 1: Contract Testing** (Interface Compatibility)

Verify extension point interfaces remain stable or provide backward-compatible changes:

```csharp
[ContractTest]
public class ClaimValidatorContractTests
{
    [Fact]
    public void IClaimValidator_InterfaceUnchanged()
    {
        // Verify interface signature matches baseline
        var currentInterface = typeof(IClaimValidator);
        var expectedMethods = new[]
        {
            "Task<ValidationResult> ValidateAsync(Claim, CancellationToken)"
        };

        var actualMethods = currentInterface.GetMethods()
            .Select(m => m.ToString())
            .ToArray();

        Assert.Equal(expectedMethods, actualMethods);
    }

    [Fact]
    public void ValidationResult_PropertiesUnchanged()
    {
        var type = typeof(ValidationResult);
        Assert.True(type.GetProperty("IsValid") != null);
        Assert.True(type.GetProperty("Errors") != null);
        Assert.True(type.GetProperty("Warnings") != null);
    }
}
```

**Level 2: Integration Testing** (Extension Execution)

Test extensions execute correctly against product:

```csharp
[IntegrationTest]
public class TexasExtensionIntegrationTests
{
    private readonly ExtensionTestHost _testHost;

    [Fact]
    public async Task TexasClaimValidator_ValidatesSuccessfully()
    {
        // Load extension in product context
        var extension = _testHost.LoadExtension<IClaimValidator>("TexasClaimValidator");

        // Execute with product data
        var claim = CreateTestClaim();
        var result = await extension.ValidateAsync(claim, CancellationToken.None);

        Assert.True(result.IsValid);
    }
}
```

**Level 3: Upgrade Simulation** (Version Compatibility)

Test extension against multiple product versions:

```csharp
[Theory]
[InlineData("2.0.0")]
[InlineData("2.1.0")]
[InlineData("2.2.0")]
public async Task Extension_CompatibleWithProductVersions(string productVersion)
{
    using var host = CreateTestHost(productVersion);
    var extension = host.LoadExtension<IClaimProcessor>("FloridaClaimProcessor");

    var result = await extension.ProcessAsync(CreateTestClaim());
    Assert.True(result.Success);
}
```

**Level 4: Compatibility Matrix** (Version Tracking)

Maintain automated matrix of tested combinations:

```
| Extension         | Product 2.0 | Product 2.1 | Product 2.2 |
|-------------------|-------------|-------------|-------------|
| Texas Claims v1.0 | ✅ Pass     | ✅ Pass     | ❌ Fail     |
| Florida Claims    | ✅ Pass     | ✅ Pass     | ✅ Pass     |
| California Provider| ⚠️ Warning | ✅ Pass     | ✅ Pass     |
```

**Level 5: Behavior Testing** (Runtime Validation)

Verify extension behavior matches expectations:

```csharp
[Fact]
public async Task Extension_MaintainsExpectedBehavior()
{
    var extension = LoadExtension();

    // Test known input/output pairs
    var result = await extension.ProcessAsync(CreateKnownInput());
    Assert.Equal(ExpectedOutput, result);

    // Test error handling
    await Assert.ThrowsAsync<ValidationException>(
        () => extension.ProcessAsync(CreateInvalidInput()));
}
```

