[patterns/application/extensions/PTN-APP-EXT-008-compatibility-testing-pattern.md#scenario-2-performance-regression-detection]

#### Scenario 2: Performance Regression Detection

**Scenario**: Product v2.2 changes data access pattern, causing extension queries to become slower.

**Detection**:

```csharp
[PerformanceTest]
public class ExtensionPerformanceTests
{
    private readonly PerformanceBenchmark _benchmark;

    [Fact]
    public async Task ClaimProcessor_MeetsPerformanceTarget()
    {
        var processor = LoadExtension<IClaimProcessor>("TexasClaimProcessor");
        var claim = TestDataRepository.CreateValidTexasClaim();

        // Baseline: v2.1 processed in 50ms
        var baseline = TimeSpan.FromMilliseconds(50);
        var tolerance = 0.10; // 10% tolerance
        var maxAllowed = baseline + TimeSpan.FromMilliseconds(baseline.TotalMilliseconds * tolerance);

        // Measure actual performance
        var stopwatch = Stopwatch.StartNew();
        for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
        {
            await processor.ProcessAsync(claim, new ProcessingContext(), CancellationToken.None);
        }
        stopwatch.Stop();

        var avgTime = TimeSpan.FromMilliseconds(stopwatch.ElapsedMilliseconds / 100.0);

        // Assert performance hasn't degraded beyond tolerance
        Assert.True(avgTime <= maxAllowed,
            $"Performance regression detected: {avgTime.TotalMilliseconds}ms (baseline: {baseline.TotalMilliseconds}ms, max: {maxAllowed.TotalMilliseconds}ms)");
    }
}
```

**Result**:
```
Test Failed: ClaimProcessor_MeetsPerformanceTarget
Performance regression detected: 82ms (baseline: 50ms, max: 55ms)

Performance Report:
  Product Version: 2.2.0
  Extension: TexasClaimProcessor
  Baseline: 50ms
  Current: 82ms
  Regression: +64% ⚠️

Root Cause Analysis:
  Product v2.2 changed DbContext query behavior
  Extension queries now execute additional round trips

Recommendation:
  - Update extension to use new .Include() pattern
  - Add caching for reference data
  - Estimated fix: reduce to 45ms
```

**Resolution**:
```csharp
// Before (slow in v2.2)
public async Task<ClaimResult> ProcessAsync(Claim claim, ...)
{
    // Multiple queries
    var provider = await _context.Providers.FindAsync(claim.ProviderId);
    var member = await _context.Members.FindAsync(claim.MemberId);
    var rules = await _context.Rules.Where(r => r.State == "Texas").ToListAsync();

    return ProcessClaim(claim, provider, member, rules);
}

// After (optimized for v2.2)
public async Task<ClaimResult> ProcessAsync(Claim claim, ...)
{
    // Single query with includes
    var claimData = await _context.Claims
        .Include(c => c.Provider)
        .Include(c => c.Member)
        .FirstOrDefaultAsync(c => c.Id == claim.Id);

    // Cached reference data
    var rules = await _ruleCache.GetTexasRulesAsync();

    return ProcessClaim(claimData, rules);
